hey this is preshtalwalker this is a  variation of a puzzle i posted about a  year ago  there is a long single file line outside  of a dance club  the first person in line is unmarried  and the last person in line is married  each person in line only looks at the  person in front of them  is a married person looking at an  unmarried person  the answer choices are yes no and cannot  be determined  surveys have found that approximately  eighty percent of people  cannot get the correct answer in a  version of this problem  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for the  solution  the short answer is that the first  person in line who is married is looking  at an unmarried person  the answer is yes  now since many people cannot get this  correct answer i'm going to go through  the logic in detail to show you why this  is true  so we'll number the people in line from  1 to n where 1 is the first person in  line and n is the last person in line  let's consider person two  if person two is married  that person two is a married person  looking at an unmarried person one in  front of them  so that would lead to the answer of yes  however we do not know whether two is  married so we have to consider that two  might be unmarried  if that is the case we then consider the  next person in line three  the logic is going to be the same  if three is a married person then three  is a married person looking at an  unmarried person to in front of them  otherwise  three is also unmarried  so we then proceed to the next person in  line four  we can continue this logic to check each  person in line  the first person that we find in line  who is married person k  is looking at an unmarried person k  minus 1 in front of them  now we may not know if any of these  people are married  in that case  all of the people in line 1 all the way  to n minus 1 are unmarried  but in that case we know the very last  person in line n  is married which means that person n is  a married person looking at an unmarried  person n minus one in front of them  therefore the answer is yes  there must be a married person looking  at an unmarried person  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on facebook google plus and  patreon you can catch me on social media  at preshellwalker and if you like this  video please check out my books there  are links in the video description
 

